# ============================================================================
# §3 — BACKEND CONVENTIONS (Django)
# ============================================================================

## 3.1 API layer
# - All new API endpoints use Django Ninja (not DRF, not raw views)
# - Schemas live in schemas.py or domain-specific schema files (e.g., transaction_schemas.py)
# - Use Pydantic models for request/response validation
# - API routes are registered in drivebase/urls.py via api.add_router()
# - Legacy views.py is maintained for PDF generation only — do NOT add new view logic there

## 3.2 Models
# - All models live in manager/models.py
# - Use gettext_lazy (_) for ALL field verbose_name values
# - Dynamic choices (vehicle types, colors, etc.) use FK to choice models, NOT CharField choices
# - Auto-generate internal_id in save() — never rely on the database pk for user-facing IDs
# - Respect unique_together constraints: [business, internal_id] is the standard pattern
# - When adding fields, ALWAYS make them nullable/blank for backwards compatibility

## 3.3 Business logic
# - Keep views/API handlers thin — complex logic belongs in model methods or service functions
# - Financial calculations MUST use Decimal, never float
# - Tax calculations: gross = net × (1 + tax_rate); net = gross / (1 + tax_rate)
# - Always handle is_no_tax flag on TaxPercentage

## 3.4 Migrations
# - Never edit an applied migration
# - Always run makemigrations and migrate after model changes
# - Test that migrations are reversible when possible

## 3.5 Security
# - CSRF is enabled on all Ninja API endpoints (csrf=True on NinjaAPI instance)
# - Session authentication — no JWT tokens
# - Rate limiting via django-ratelimit on sensitive endpoints
# - Never expose email, password hashes, or approval_tokens in API responses
# - Filter querysets by request.user.business — no exceptions


# ============================================================================
# §4 — FRONTEND CONVENTIONS (React + TypeScript)
# ============================================================================

## 4.1 File organization
# - Pages go in src/pages/ (one file per page)
# - Reusable components in src/components/ (organized by domain: ui/, layout/, vehicles/, etc.)
# - Custom hooks in src/hooks/ (one hook per file, prefixed with "use")
# - API client config in src/lib/api.ts
# - Auth context in src/lib/auth.tsx
# - Validation schemas in src/lib/validations.ts or src/schemas/

## 4.2 Component patterns
# - Use functional components only (no class components)
# - shadcn/ui + Radix UI for all interactive primitives
# - TailwindCSS for styling — no inline styles, no CSS modules
# - All user-facing text MUST use the t() function from react-i18next
# - Never hardcode German strings — always use translation keys

## 4.3 Data fetching
# - Use TanStack Query (useQuery, useMutation) for all API calls
# - Custom hooks wrap TanStack Query (useVehicles, useTransactions, etc.)
# - Axios instance in lib/api.ts handles CSRF token injection and base URL
# - Never use raw fetch() — always use the configured Axios instance

## 4.4 Forms
# - React Hook Form + Zod for all forms
# - Validation schemas use Zod and live in schemas/ or lib/validations.ts
# - Auto-save via useAutoSave hook where appropriate

## 4.5 Routing
# - React Router v7 with URL pattern: /:business_slug/:locale/...
# - Locale defaults to 'de' when omitted from URL
# - All protected routes wrapped in <ProtectedRoute />
# - Auth routes use <PublicRoute /> + <AuthLayout />

## 4.6 State management
# - Server state: TanStack Query (never duplicate in local state)
# - Auth state: React Context (AuthProvider)
# - UI state: useState / useReducer (local)
# - URL state: useParams / useSearchParams
# - Do NOT introduce Zustand, Redux, or other state libraries without explicit approval

## 4.7 TypeScript
# - Strict mode enabled
# - No `any` types — use `unknown` and narrow
# - Prefer interfaces for object shapes, types for unions
# - All API response types defined in src/types/


# ============================================================================
# §5 — INTERNATIONALIZATION (i18n)
# ============================================================================

## 5.1 Supported locales
# de (German — default), en (English), tr (Turkish), ar (Arabic — RTL)

## 5.2 Frontend
# - Translation files: src/locales/{de,en,tr,ar}.json
# - ALL user-visible strings must use t('key') — no hardcoded text
# - New features must add keys to ALL four locale files
# - Arabic triggers RTL layout via document.documentElement.dir = 'rtl'

## 5.3 Backend
# - Model fields use gettext_lazy (_) for verbose_name
# - Translation files in backend/locale/ (.po/.mo)
# - Rosetta UI available at /rosetta/ for managing translations


# ============================================================================
# §6 — PDF GENERATION
# ============================================================================

## 6.1 General rules
# - All PDFs use ReportLab
# - PDF generators live in backend/manager/views.py (legacy) and pdf_helpers.py
# - German number-to-words via num2words library
# - PDFs include: business logo, full address, bank details, tax IDs
# - Never change existing PDF layout without explicit user approval

## 6.2 Document types
# - Kaufvertrag (Sale Contract)
# - Verbindliche Bestellung (Binding Order)
# - Verkaufvertrag (Purchase Agreement)
# - Quittung (Receipt) — includes price in German words
# - Identitätsprüfung (Identity Check)
# - Transaktionsbeleg (Transaction Receipt)


# ============================================================================
# §7 — CODE QUALITY & SAFETY
# ============================================================================

## 7.1 Before committing
# - Backend: python manage.py test manager.tests (all tests must pass)
# - Frontend: npm run build (TypeScript must compile without errors)
# - Never commit .env files, db.sqlite3, node_modules, or __pycache__

## 7.2 Naming conventions
# - Python: snake_case for variables/functions, PascalCase for classes
# - TypeScript: camelCase for variables/functions, PascalCase for components/types
# - Database columns: snake_case (Django default)
# - API endpoints: kebab-case in URLs
# - Translation keys: dot.separated.camelCase (e.g., vehicles.addNew)

## 7.3 Comments & documentation
# - Preserve ALL existing comments and docstrings unless explicitly told to remove them
# - Add docstrings to new Django model methods and API endpoints
# - Never delete TODO/FIXME comments — they track known technical debt

## 7.4 Error handling
# - Backend: raise appropriate HTTP exceptions (400, 401, 403, 404, 422)
# - Frontend: show user-friendly error messages via toast/alert
# - Never silently swallow errors

## 7.5 Git hygiene
# - Write clear, descriptive commit messages
# - One logical change per commit
# - Never force-push to shared branches


# ============================================================================
# §8 — THINGS YOU MUST NEVER DO
# ============================================================================

# ❌ Never expose data from one business to another (multi-tenant violation)
# ❌ Never use float for money — always Decimal
# ❌ Never hardcode German text in React — always use i18n translation keys
# ❌ Never add a new state management library without approval
# ❌ Never delete or rename existing API endpoints without a migration plan
# ❌ Never edit applied Django migrations
# ❌ Never commit secrets, API keys, or passwords to the repository
# ❌ Never use raw SQL without parameterized queries
# ❌ Never skip CSRF protection on mutation endpoints
# ❌ Never return password hashes, approval tokens, or session IDs in API responses
# ❌ Never use `any` in TypeScript
# ❌ Never remove existing comments/docstrings unless explicitly asked
